ZERO.EXECUTION / language-native protocol

INPUT
  A field is a finite or open sequence of traces.

STATE
  trace := form + relation + history + pressure + age
  No semantic type is assigned.

TRANSITION
  A transition is accepted only when it changes the observable field.
  Multiple transitions may coexist.
  A transition may be reversed, contradicted, delayed or forgotten.

DISCOVERY
  The machine may create a candidate relation from observed changes.
  Candidate relations are provisional.
  A candidate must reproduce across independent fields before promotion.

TRANSFER
  Replace symbols while preserving structural conditions.
  A valid discovery must survive symbol replacement.
  A failure remains recorded.

SELF-EXTENSION
  A candidate may propose a new primitive.
  The primitive becomes executable only after blind validation.

ADVERSARY
  Every promoted relation receives an opposing trajectory.
  Survival against the adversary is part of the result.

UNKNOWN
  Missing information remains represented as unknown.
  Unknown is never silently converted into a guessed value.

MEASUREMENT
  Record trajectory, transformations, transfer, failures, discovery, time and resource use.

HUMAN-OVERRIDE
  None. Human interpretation is external to execution.

VERDICT
  No claim of superiority is allowed without unseen evaluation, independent reproduction, human calibration and measurable margin.